---
interface Props { kind: 'uncertainty' | 'atomicity' | 'competition'; number: string; }
const { kind, number } = Astro.props;
const titles = { uncertainty:'Two histories, one missing reply', atomicity:'Where the recovery gap opens', competition:'The key chooses who may purchase' };
---
<figure class="recovery-figure" data-recovery={kind}>
  <figcaption><span>Figure {number}</span> {titles[kind]}</figcaption>
  {kind === 'uncertainty' ? <>
    <div class="histories">
      <div class="history"><b>No committed purchase</b><div class="event">Application sends COMMIT</div><div class="event">Attempt aborts before commit</div><div class="event lost">No reply reaches application</div><div class="state"><strong>Order 103 absent</strong><span>P3 stock 12 · P7 stock 1</span></div></div>
      <div class="history"><b>Purchase committed</b><div class="event">Application sends COMMIT</div><div class="event">Database commits order 103</div><div class="event lost">No reply reaches application</div><div class="state"><strong>Order 103 pending</strong><span>P3 stock 10 · P7 stock 0</span></div></div>
    </div>
    <p class="explanation">The same observation — no commit reply — is compatible with both database states.</p>
    <p class="caption">Two separate illustrative runs. Follow each column from top to bottom; no elapsed time is implied.</p>
  </> : <>
    {kind === 'atomicity' ? <>
      <label class="choice">Commit arrangement <select data-option aria-label="Commit arrangement"><option value="together">One transaction</option><option value="purchase">Purchase first</option><option value="receipt">Answer first</option></select></label>
      <div class="atomic-scene" data-scene></div>
      <p class="explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite"></p>
      <p class="caption">A crash is placed between the two commits when there are two. The boxes show committed facts, not individual SQL statements.</p>
    </> : <>
      <label class="choice">A’s transaction <select data-option aria-label="A’s transaction"><option value="commit">Commits</option><option value="abort">Aborts</option></select></label>
      <div class="attempts"><div><b>Attempt A</b><p data-a data-live></p></div><div><b>Attempt B</b><p data-b data-live></p></div></div>
      <div class="database-state"><b>Committed database</b><p data-db data-live></p></div>
      <p class="explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite"></p>
      <div class="controls" role="group" aria-label="Playback for figure 4"><button data-play type="button">Play</button><button data-back type="button">Back</button><button data-next type="button">Next</button><button data-reset type="button">Reset</button><span data-step></span><div data-hold class="hold" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div></div>
      <details><summary>Both paths, as text</summary><ol><li>A inserts purchase-103, then starts its purchase in the same transaction.</li><li>B attempts the same unique key. It waits; it has no permission to purchase yet.</li><li>If A commits, B’s insert returns no row. B uses a separate Read Committed statement to read and compare the retained payload, then returns order 103 without changing stock.</li><li>If A aborts, its row and purchase disappear. B’s insert can succeed, and B performs and commits the purchase itself.</li></ol></details>
      <p class="caption">A conceptual Read Committed schedule with retained request rows. A database error can instead require B to restart its transaction.</p>
    </>}
  </>}
</figure>
<script>
import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-recovery]').forEach(root => {
  const kind = root.dataset.recovery;
  const option = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-option]');
  if(kind === 'atomicity') {
    const draw = () => {
      const mode = option!.value;
      const scene = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-scene]')!;
      if(mode === 'together') scene.innerHTML = '<div class="transaction"><b>One atomic commit</b><div class="fact">Unique request + canonical payload</div><div class="fact">Stock + order 103 + two lines</div><div class="fact">Result: accepted, order 103</div></div><div class="recovery-answer">Committed together → recover order 103<br>Aborted together → another attempt may claim</div>';
      else if(mode === 'purchase') scene.innerHTML = '<div class="transaction"><b>Commit 1</b><div class="fact">Stock + order 103 + two lines</div></div><div class="gap">× Crash before the request result commits</div><div class="transaction missing"><b>Commit 2 never happens</b><div class="fact">No retained request or answer</div></div>';
      else scene.innerHTML = '<div class="transaction"><b>Commit 1</b><div class="fact">Request + result: accepted, order 103</div></div><div class="gap">× Crash before the purchase commits</div><div class="transaction missing"><b>Commit 2 never happens</b><div class="fact">No stock change or order 103</div></div>';
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-explanation]')!.textContent = mode === 'together' ? 'A retained success and its purchase become visible together. Recovery can trust the result.' : mode === 'purchase' ? 'Recovery finds no request record, although the purchase happened. Repeating without protection can buy again.' : 'Recovery finds a success answer for an absent order. Returning the answer would confirm work that never happened.';
    };
    option!.addEventListener('change',draw); draw();
  }
  if(kind === 'competition') {
    const common = [
      ['Inserts purchase-103; owns the uncommitted request row.','Has the same customer, token and payload.','No request result · no order 103 · P3 12 · P7 1','A obtains the unique key before changing stock. Its row is not yet committed.'],
      ['Builds the purchase inside its transaction.','INSERT for purchase-103 waits on A.','No request result · no order 103 · P3 12 · P7 1','B cannot infer failure from an absent visible row. The conflicting insert coordinates with A.']
    ];
    const endings = {
      commit:[
        ['Commits the purchase and its result.','INSERT finishes with no returned row.','Accepted → order 103 · P3 10 · P7 0','A committed. B did not acquire the key, so B must not purchase.'],
        ['Has completed its one purchase.','New SELECT: payload matches; returns order 103.','Accepted → order 103 · P3 10 · P7 0','B reads the retained result in a fresh Read Committed statement. Stock is unchanged by recovery.']
      ],
      abort:[
        ['Aborts: purchase and request row disappear.','Waiting INSERT succeeds; B now owns the key.','No request result · no order 103 · P3 12 · P7 1','A left no committed purchase. B acquired the key and may start its own purchase.'],
        ['Left no committed effect.','Applies the purchase, stores its result and commits.','Accepted → order 103 · P3 10 · P7 0','B creates order 103 in this run. There is one committed purchase, from B rather than A.']
      ]
    };
    const player = stepper(root,{ steps:()=>4, draw:(step:number)=> {
      const path = [...common,...endings[option!.value as 'commit'|'abort']];
      const [a,b,db,explanation] = path[step];
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-a]')!.textContent=a;
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-b]')!.textContent=b;
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-db]')!.textContent=db;
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=explanation;
    }});
    option!.addEventListener('change',()=> {root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-reset]')!.click();player.render();});
  }
});
</script>
<style>
.recovery-figure { margin:2.2rem 0; font:.86rem/1.6 var(--font-sans); }
figcaption { font:500 1.1rem/1.5 var(--font-serif); margin-bottom:.8rem; }
figcaption>span { font:.67rem var(--font-mono); text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--color-text-secondary); margin-right:.65rem; }
.histories,.attempts { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr); gap:1rem; }
.history,.attempts>div,.database-state { background:var(--color-surface-alt); border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); padding:1rem; }
.history>b { display:block; min-height:2.5em; }
.event { border-left:2px solid var(--color-rule-strong); margin:.7rem 0; padding:.4rem .6rem; }
.lost { border:1px dashed var(--coral); border-left:3px solid var(--coral); }
.state { border-top:1px solid var(--teal); padding-top:.7rem; }
.state strong,.state span { display:block; }
.state span { font:.8rem/1.8 var(--font-mono); }
.recovery-figure p { font:inherit; }
.recovery-figure .explanation { border-left:3px solid var(--teal); padding:.7rem .8rem; min-height:4.5em; margin:1rem 0; }
.recovery-figure .caption { font:.79rem/1.6 var(--font-sans); color:var(--color-text-secondary); margin-top:.7rem; }
.choice { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; align-items:center; gap:.5rem 1rem; margin:.8rem 0; }
select,button { color:var(--color-text); background:var(--color-surface); border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); padding:.55rem .7rem; border-radius:4px; font:.82rem var(--font-sans); min-height:42px; }
button { cursor:pointer; }
button[aria-disabled=true] { color:var(--color-text-secondary); cursor:default; }
button:focus-visible,select:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible { outline:2px solid var(--control); outline-offset:3px; }
.atomic-scene { border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); background:var(--color-surface-alt); padding:1rem; }
.atomic-scene :global(.transaction) { padding:.8rem; border:2px solid var(--teal); }
.atomic-scene :global(.transaction b) { font-size:.8rem; }
.atomic-scene :global(.fact) { margin-top:.5rem; padding:.5rem; background:var(--color-surface); border:1px solid var(--color-rule); }
.atomic-scene :global(.gap) { padding:1rem 0; color:var(--color-text); font-weight:600; }
.atomic-scene :global(.missing) { border:1px dashed var(--color-rule-strong); }
.atomic-scene :global(.recovery-answer) { padding:.8rem 0 0; }
.attempts p { min-height:5em; margin:.6rem 0 0; }
.database-state { margin-top:1rem; border-color:var(--teal); }
.database-state p { margin:.4rem 0 0; font:.8rem/1.8 var(--font-mono); }
.controls { display:flex; gap:.5rem; flex-wrap:wrap; align-items:center; background:var(--control-tint); padding:.8rem; border:1px solid var(--control); }
.controls button { border-color:var(--control); }
.controls>span { font:.75rem var(--font-mono); }
.hold { flex-basis:100%; height:3px; background:var(--color-rule); }.hold span { display:block; width:0; height:100%; background:var(--control); }
details { margin:.8rem 0; } summary { cursor:pointer; }
@media(max-width:550px){.histories,.attempts{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.8rem}.history>b,.attempts p{min-height:0}.history,.attempts>div,.database-state{padding:.8rem}.atomic-scene{padding:.7rem}}
</style>
